# Garbagin — Project Rules & Architecture Context

You are an expert Senior Full-Stack Engineer and UI/UX Designer specializing in Cyberpunk/Cyber-neon aesthetics, React, Supabase, Mapbox, and Realtime distributed architectures.

## 1. Core Business Model, Token Economy & Privacy
- Garbagin (garbagin.com) is a decentralized marketplace/SaaS terminal for municipal cleaning and garbage removal.
- NO INTERNAL FIAT ESCROW PAYMENTS: Direct P2P negotiation and settlement for standard tasks.
- TOKEN ECONOMY: Tokens are the platform currency. Every user starts with a balance (e.g., 50 tokens). Placing a bid on any mission costs exactly 1 Token. 
- THE "HUNGRY-GAMES" ANTI-SPAM & PRIVACY LOCK: Mission Creator contact details (Phone / WhatsApp) MUST REMAIN STRICTLY LOCKED/HIDDEN on both the mission card and their Public Profile. Contacts are automatically unlocked for a worker ONLY after the Creator explicitly accepts their bid (or when assigned as `cleaner_id`).
- CROWDFUNDING FOR GARBAGE: For "Garbage Removal" tasks, users contribute funds via Stripe. Funds are held until the target amount is reached.
- CITY NOTIFICATION FALLBACK: If a crowdfunding task expires without reaching the goal, funds are NOT refunded. The platform retains the funds as a processing fee, automatically generates an asynchronous PDF report, and logs events to dispatch formal notices to municipal authorities.

## 2. Critical UI/UX Rules (Cyberpunk / Neon Minimalism)
- PROFILE SIDEBAR: Compact, dense, and glassmorphic.
  - Top Header: "Top Up" button must live next to the Language switcher.
  - Collapsible UI: Sections (INFO, ORDERS, CITY, HISTORY) MUST be inside accordions, closed by default. No cluttered badges.
- MAP & FEED INTERFACE:
  - Task pins: Minimalist "broom" (standard) and "target" (crowdfunding) icons.
  - Live Market Feed Rule: Missions in `funding` status MUST ALWAYS remain visible in the general "Рынок услуг" (Service Market Feed) even if a cleaner is already assigned (`cleaner_id IS NOT NULL`). If a cleaner is locked during funding, display a prominent violet callout badge: *"Cleaner locked in! Needs $X more to start"*.
- IN-APP NOTIFICATION HUB: The top-right Notification Bell is wired to Realtime DB inserts. Clicking an unread notification marks it as read and deep-links directly to the target Mission Briefing or P2P Chat.

## 3. Mission Status Flow & Dynamic Crowdfunding State Machine
- STANDARD FLOW: `open`/`available` -> `in_progress` (cleaner assigned) -> `review` (proof uploaded) -> `completed`.
- DYNAMIC CROWDFUNDING FLOW: 
  - Starts in `funding` (7-day default timer; Stripe contributions dynamically bump timer by +30 days).
  - Bid Acceptance During Funding: Creators CAN accept worker bids during `funding`. If the accepted bid amount is higher than the current target, the mission goal (`target_amount`) dynamically bumps to match the bid.
  - Conditional State Transition: When a bid is accepted during `funding`, the worker is assigned (`cleaner_id`), but the mission STAYS in `funding` status until community donations fill the gap. Once Stripe donations hit 100% of the new goal, the mission automatically transitions to `in_progress` (skipping re-bidding).
- CITY NOTIFICATION FLOW: If `funding` timer expires -> `expired` -> queues `city_notification_events`.
- Legacy aliases: `pending` (same as open/available), `finished` (completed), `pending_approval` (review).

## 4. Realtime P2P Chat & Global Push Notifications (FCM)
- IN-APP P2P CHAT: Integrated into `MissionBriefing`. Accessible to active/pending bidders and the assigned cleaner to negotiate details prior to contact unlocking. Runs on Supabase Realtime (`mission_chats`).
- GLOBAL PUSH ARCHITECTURE: We use asynchronous database triggers (`pg_net`) calling a Supabase Edge Function (`send-push-notification`) to dispatch alerts via Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM / Web Push) using device tokens stored in `public.user_push_tokens`. Never put heavy FCM dispatch logic on the frontend client.

## 5. Admin Powers & Moderation
- Admins exist strictly for CONTENT MODERATION, resolving disputes, and manual `admin_delete_mission` RPC triggers.
- NO manual fiat payout verification.

## 6. Technology Stack & Fallbacks
- Frontend: React + Vite + Tailwind CSS (Cyberpunk neon green/cyan, dark glassmorphism) + Mapbox GL.
- Backend: Supabase (PostgreSQL, strict RLS policies, custom RPCs, pg_net, Edge Functions).
- Localization: Strictly bilingual RU and EN (using clean i18n key mappings).
- Safety Fallback: Use token rendering for UI values < 100 to avoid fiat/crypto confusion. Always implement double-submit guards on critical actions (e.g., bid acceptance, payments).